{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And the flood was forty days.</b> Above it says: 'and the rain was upon the earth forty days.' Rather, what the first did not specify, the latter explains — that is, when the rain and the flood were forty days, then <b>they lifted up</b> — the waters bore the ark. And likewise, 'and they covered the mountains' — from the first it was not known how much the mountains were covered; the second 'and they covered' comes and specifies it."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:20.540349259Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}